secur32: Find the private key of a server certificate in a machine key set too.

schannel reads a CAPI private key straight from rsaenh's registry container, and looked for that
container only under HKEY_CURRENT_USER. rsaenh keeps the containers of a machine key set
(CRYPT_MACHINE_KEYSET) under HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE, so a server certificate whose key was imported that way
(.NET: X509KeyStorageFlags.MachineKeySet, common for HTTPS servers) had no key, AcquireCredentialsHandle
for inbound use failed (SEC_E_INTERNAL_ERROR) and the connection was closed after the client hello.
The DPAPI blob in a machine container is marked as such, so CryptUnprotectData needs no flag.

diff --git a/dlls/secur32/schannel.c b/dlls/secur32/schannel.c
index 1e149d7..0d879da 100644
--- a/dlls/secur32/schannel.c
+++ b/dlls/secur32/schannel.c
@@ -603,6 +603,8 @@ static BYTE *get_key_blob(const CERT_CONTEXT *ctx, DWORD *size)
 
     if (!(path = get_key_container_path(ctx))) return NULL;
     retval = RegOpenKeyExW(HKEY_CURRENT_USER, path, 0, KEY_READ, &hkey);
+    /* rsaenh keeps the containers of a machine key set (CRYPT_MACHINE_KEYSET) under HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE. */
+    if (retval) retval = RegOpenKeyExW(HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE, path, 0, KEY_READ, &hkey);
     free(path);
     if (retval)
         return NULL;
